+# Consolidated owner-confirmation checklist
+
+Prepared 2 November 2026. Pending items are not implemented as new facts or visible placeholders. Lucknow remains the primary market. Confirm facts once using business records, then approve a separate consistent correction across visible content, schema and external profiles.
+
+| Item | Current evidence / conflict | Owner confirmation needed | Publication treatment |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Office address and PIN | Public text/schema retain 227107; earlier owner input specified 226101 for Kakori/Pili Market | Correct staffed/customer-visit address, postal PIN and signage | Address/PIN unchanged here; no guessed coordinates |
+| Maps identity | OfficeMap and Contact use https://maps.google.com/?cid=5167156942475472384 | Verify that this is the intended business listing and directions destination | No Maps/GBP edit or inferred location |
+| YouTube identity | Footer links https://www.youtube.com/@visionsecure_tech; Contact links https://www.youtube.com/@vishalkumar9004 | Which channel represents the business and is controlled by it? | No guessed sameAs or account replacement |
+| Real coverage | Lucknow is the established site focus | Confirm actual localities and the requested Hardoi, Raebareli, Kanpur, Unnao, Sitapur, Barabanki and Varanasi markets: installation staff, travel, repeat visits and support | Requested expansion is not proof of an office, regular coverage or projects; no city pages/lists added |
+| Site visit / consultation | Existing promotional labels elsewhere refer to free visits/consultation; terms have not been established | Visit availability, travel/assessment charges, conditions and whether any free offer is actually available | FAQ now asks customers to confirm charges; no new free offer or fixed fee |
+| Warranty and AMC | Contract-specific evidence not supplied | Product warranty, claim route, covered tasks, visit frequency, spares/labour, exclusions, remote/onsite access and response commitments | No universal warranty duration, quarterly/unlimited support or response-time promise |
+| Supported models and special work | Generic catalogue and enquiry options do not establish every device/integration | Brands/models, repair capability, software/licences and specific Fire Alarm, EPABX, doorbell/intercom scope | Conditional assessment only; no invented dealership, certification or compliance service |
+| Credentials and partnerships | Existing site has partner/experience/verification-style marketing claims without supplied evidence | Current certifications, permission to claim partnerships and actual professional responsibilities | No new credential; removed the article sidebar's unsupported Verified label |
+| Testimonials and projects | Existing gallery/project/review copy was not independently authenticated in this task | Real work, dates, customer consent, photo ownership and permission to publish names/results | No new customer, project, testimonial or result fabricated |
+| Article identity and dates | Existing articles display a team label and historical dates | Verify authorship/publication history and any later qualified technical review | Article schema omits unverified authors/review/modified dates; no fake freshness |
+| Business policies | The task supplies no complete approved privacy/terms policy | Confirm actual data handling, retention and customer terms before publishing policy copy | No legal policy or assurance invented for an audit score |
+
+## Separate popup proposal - not implemented
+
+The existing automatic popup opens after its original 4-second timer and can interrupt mobile reading. At 390x844 the form is scrollable, the submit control is reachable, Tab remains inside the dialog, Escape closes it and the session flag prevents repeated opening. No timing, trigger, lead validation or submission behavior changed.
+
+If desired, approve a later controlled experiment using a user-engagement trigger or longer reading opportunity, retaining the ordinary enquiry CTA. Define consent, qualified-enquiry and usability measurements before choosing a trigger. Do not hide or delay the popup merely to inflate a performance test.
